.TH COREINJECT 1 "2016-07-19" "minicoredumper" "minicoredumper"
.
.SH NAME
coreinject \- inject binary dumps from
.BR minicoredumper (8)
into a
.BR core (5)
file
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coreinject
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIcore\fR
.I symbol.map
.IR binary-dump ...
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
If an application using
.BR libminicoredumper (7)
registers a binary dump to not be included in the
.BR core (5)
file, the
.BR minicoredumper (8)
will generate a separate binary dump file containing the contents of that
variable. A symbol map file
.I symbol.map
is also created by the
.BR minicoredumper (8).
Using these files,
.B coreinject
can inject that binary data into the stripped
.BR core (5)
file for use with
.BR gdb (1).
.PP
The options are as follows:
.TP
\fB--data=\fIIDENT\fR:\fISIZE\fR@\fISRCFILE\fR+\fISRCOFF\fR
Inject
.I SIZE
bytes of data at offset
.I SRCOFF
of file
.I SRCFILE
to the
.BR core (5).
The data is injected at the location of the
.I IDENT
as stored in the symbol map. This option is useful for injecting data
other than that which was actually dumped by the
.BR minicoredumper (8).
.IP
If a
.I binary-dump
for the same
.I IDENT
is also specified as an argument, the data from the
.I --data
argument takes precedence. Specifying both is useful if the
.I IDENT
was registered with
.IR MCD_DATA_PTR_INDIRECT .
The indirect (pointer) data would come from the
.I binary-dump
and the direct data would come from the
.I --data
.IR SRCFILE .
.
.SH NOTES
If the binary dump used
.IR MCD_DATA_PTR_DIRECT ,
the separate binary file
contains exactly that data. If
.I MCD_DATA_PTR_INDIRECT
was used, the separate binary dump file contains first the pointer value
followed by the data pointed to by the pointer.
.
.SH EXAMPLE
Assuming binary data was registered with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mcd_dump_data_t dd;
unsigned long val;

mcd_dump_data_register_bin("bdump.bin", 6, &dd, &val, sizeof(val),
                           MCD_DATA_PTR_DIRECT | MCD_LENGTH_DIRECT);
.fi
.RE
.PP
Using the generated symbol map file
.IR symbol.map ,
insert the binary data dumped to
.I bdump.bin
into the generated
.BR core (5)
file.
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ coreinject core symbol.map bdump.bin
.fi
.RE
.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR minicoredumper (8),
.BR libminicoredumper (7),
.BR mcd_dump_data_register_bin (3)
.PP
